| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Elijah found him plowing [Eb]deep
[Bb]Twelve yoke of oxen by his [Eb]feet
[Gm]He threw his cloak [F]across the [Eb]boy
[Gm]Elisha left [F]the team to [Eb]go
[Cm7]He killed the oxen and ate with [Eb]all
[Cm7]Then followed on to serve them [F]all
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]A double por[F]tion of the spir[Eb]it
[Bb]Given to [F]the prophet's [Eb]heir
The [Gm]chariot of [F]fire rose a[Eb]bove
And he re[F]ceived the pow[Eb]er
to [Bb]cross
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Naaman came with silver and [Eb]gold
[Bb]A mighty man with lepro[Eb]sy [Gm]told
Wash seven [F]times in the Jordan [Eb]stream
[Gm]His flesh returned [F]like a young boy's [Eb]dream
[Cm7]The widow's jar of [Bb/D]oil was [Eb]full
[Cm7]She sold the oil to keep them [F]whole
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]The Shunammite's son lay on the [Eb]bed
[Bb]Elisha prayed inside the [F]shed
[Gm]He lay on him and breathed his [Eb]life
[Cm7]The boy sneezed seven times and opened [Eb]eyes
[Cm7]The Syrian army was [Bb/D]struck with [Eb]blind
[Cm7]Led to Samaria for a feast of [F]kind
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm]Where is the [F]God of Eli[Eb]jah
The waters [F]divide to the right and [Bb]left
{end_of_verse}

